// Title: Remote Access Tool - MeshAgent Command Execution via MeshCentral
// Sigma ID: 74a2b202-73e0-4693-9a3a-9d36146d0775
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @Kostastsale
// Date: 2024-09-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: Detects the use of MeshAgent to execute commands on the target host, particularly when threat
//   actors might abuse it to execute commands directly. MeshAgent can execute commands on the target
//   host by leveraging win-console to obscure their activities and win-dispatcher to run malicious
//   code through IPC with child processes.
// False positives:
//   - False positives can be found in environments using MeshAgent for remote management, analysis should prioritize the grandparent process, MeshAgent.exe, and scrutinize the resulting child processes triggered by any suspicious interactive commands directed at the target host.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Ylianst/MeshAgent
//   - https://github.com/Ylianst/MeshAgent/blob/52cf129ca43d64743181fbaf940e0b4ddb542a37/modules/win-dispatcher.js#L173
//   - https://github.com/Ylianst/MeshAgent/blob/52cf129ca43d64743181fbaf940e0b4ddb542a37/modules/win-info.js#L55
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_meshagent_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\meshagent.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe")
